From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMyGlass <openmyglass@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:34:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: interactive: default io_is_busy to 1

On the Glass glass-omap-xrx13b kernel (3.4), get_cpu_idle_time_us()
excludes iowait, so the stock interactive governor counts iowait as
busy time. The io_is_busy backport defaults to 0, which would count
iowait as idle and change how the tuned build measures load.

Default io_is_busy to 1 so that the tuned build keeps the stock
accounting. Writing 0 to
/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/interactive/io_is_busy still selects
the upstream behaviour, for measurement.

This change is licensed under GPL-2.0-only, like the file it changes.
---
 drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c
index d1e8b86..85d2108 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@ static u64 boostpulse_endtime;
 #define DEFAULT_TIMER_SLACK (4 * DEFAULT_TIMER_RATE)
 static int timer_slack_val = DEFAULT_TIMER_SLACK;
 
-static bool io_is_busy;
+static bool io_is_busy = true;
 
 static int cpufreq_governor_interactive(struct cpufreq_policy *policy,
 		unsigned int event);
